| g4-data-people: who collects data about people, and who could be helped or hurt | 3 | g5-data-benefits-risks | Benefits and risks of a technology that uses collected data |
| g4-trace-values: values traced through a program in a trace-table | 4 | g5-variables-use | Variables stored, compared and changed |
| g4-compare-solutions: two programs with one result compared for correctness and clarity | 4 | g5-remix-program | A working program modified and combined with another, credited |
| g4-debug-increment: build and test in small pieces, with the test-table | 4 | g5-systematic-debug | Three debugging strategies compared |
| g4-team-document: a team program with each member's part and its comment | 4 | g5-team-project | Components built by each student and described for the others |
| g4-ml-learning: training data's properties change a sorter's output; how people and machines learn differently | 5 | g5-train-model; g5-use-or-not | A small classifier trained on a device; when a computer is the right tool |
| g4-history-limits: diverse people and communities in computing's history; limits that led to new tools | 5 | g5-use-or-not; g5-who-included | When a technology fits; who was left out or included in making a tool |
| g4-work-tools: how workers learn new computing tools and keep learning | 5 | g5-professionals | How a team of roles builds one tool |

Every row above is named in the grade 5 row's assumes, and each grade 4 row names the grade 5 rows in its hands_on.

