data,12,g12-data-policy-debate,HS-DAT-IM-28; S1-DSC-PP-13,g11-policy-change; g11-data-scale-ethics,,benefit-risk-chart,benefit-risk-chart,policy; regulation; responsible use; debate; efficacy; evidence; law; claim,ela:e12-seminar,"Unplugged day. A structured debate on how well a data policy or regulation (a rule on consent, on retention, on sharing) works to keep data use responsible, with two prepared sides and dated sources. Students judge efficacy against the evidence, not against their side. The written preparation can serve the ELA seminar. Paper path: prepared cards and a scoring sheet. Model carried: benefit-risk-chart. Cases are from memory, to be checked before use. Specialty I addition (S1-DSC-PP-13): the debate cases include how collecting and using data affects groups that are under-represented or marginalized, with evidence for each effect named. The debate also weighs social approaches (a public campaign, people changing their own habits) beside the rule, and the Specialty I cases end with one way to collect a fairer dataset."
