| Data and information: Flat-file databases | 1 Creating a paper-based database; 2 Computer databases; 3 Using a database | Unit 3, session 1 | Records on paper first, then the same records in the table tool, one row a record and one column an attribute, and a column sorted | None of 1 to 3 |
| Data and information: Flat-file databases | 4 Using search tools | None | | Left out: searching with conditions is past E4-DAT-DC-09; offered to grade 6 (g6-sort-filter-tool) |
| Data and information: Flat-file databases | 5 Comparing data visually; 6 Databases in real life | Unit 3, sessions 2 and 4 | Lesson 5: a chart made from the table to answer a question (session 2); lesson 6: data held about people in the real world, as the case-card session (session 4) | None of 5 and 6 |
| Programming B: Selection in quizzes | 1 Exploring conditions; 2 Selecting outcomes | Unit 4, session 1 | The quiz's condition and its outcomes, traced with the score in a trace-table; selection as review of grade 3 | None of 1 and 2 |
