| g5-variables-use: store, compare and update a variable, traced first | 3 | g6-variable-types | Variables of different types |
| g5-systematic-debug: three strategies with a test-table, the strategy named | 3 | g6-verify-algorithm | Testing an algorithm against expected results |
| g5-remix-program: a novel program from existing parts, credited in a comment | 3 | g6-procedures | Reusable procedures, in blocks and Python text side by side |
| g5-team-project: individual components, documented, assembled and tested by a non-author | 3 | g6-inclusive-collab | Inclusive collaboration on a shared program |
| g5-collect-tools: numeric and descriptive data collected and organized with a tool | 4 | g6-precision-metadata; g6-sort-filter-tool | Precision and metadata; sorting and filtering in a tool |
| g5-variability: typical values, outliers and possible sources of difference | 4 | g6-data-quality | Judging data quality |
| g5-train-model: a model trained, tested and retrained after a look at who or what is missing | 4 | g6-ml-hypothesis | A hypothesis about a model's behavior, tested |
| g5-data-benefits-risks: a benefit-risk-chart for a technology that uses collected data | 4 | g6-data-about-people | Data about people, its uses and limits |
| g5-hardware-software: input, processing, storage and output on the system-diagram | 1 | g6-compare-systems; g6-devices-industry | Compare systems; devices in industry |
| g5-network-parts: the parts of wired and wireless networks | 1 | g6-packets | Messages as packets across a network |
| g5-cia-triad: confidentiality, integrity and availability on the cia-triangle | 1 | g6-cia-practice | The triangle used on security practices |
| g5-who-included: inclusion and exclusion shaping tools; culture, living and work | 5 | g6-computing-eras | Eras of computing on the timeline |
| g5-use-or-not: when to use computing, and how people choose | 5 | g6-human-decisions | Decisions people keep and decisions given to systems |
| g5-professionals: professionals collaborating with shared digital tools | 5 | g6-careers-ct | Careers and computational thinking |

Every hand-on above is answered by that row's assumes in data/progressions/computer-science.csv. Grade 6 meets two
or three times a week and starts Python beside blocks (STANDARD.md "Blocks to text"), so grade 5's programs stay in
blocks with their text view; the grade 6 frame bridges to text. Each grade 6 row opens as a retrieval task, since
grade 5 is the year before.

