titles and unit overviews), opened 2026-11-25; each archived Year 6 unit lists six lessons. The publisher teaches each
unit's lessons in number order; where this frame splits a unit or takes part of it, the row says why. Each adapted
lesson keeps its idea, is rewritten in our words for an American grade 5, replaces the named block language,
spreadsheet and board with our own editor, a table tool and paper, and is credited once a day. Check days are ours,
never a kept lesson.

